From: =?UTF-8?q?N=C3=ADcolas=20F=2E=20R=2E=20A=2E=20Prado?=
 <nfraprado@collabora.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 15:41:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 134/188] drm/amd/display: Always notify the HDA driver on
 disconnect
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

amdgpu_dm_audio_eld_notify() is currently only called in atomic commits.
This results in the state of the HDA driver never getting updated when
an audio sink is removed and an atomic commit never comes. (eg the HDMI
audio jack switch in ALSA stays 'on' after the HDMI cable is
disconnected if no other display is connected to cause the compositor to
submit an atomic commit)

Call amdgpu_dm_audio_eld_notify() in the disconnect case of
amdgpu_dm_update_connector_after_detect() to ensure that the HDA driver
always gets notified on disconnect regardless of atomic commits.

Assisted-by: Copilot:claude-sonnet-4.6
Signed-off-by: Nícolas F. R. A. Prado <nfraprado@collabora.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
index be1d99d01..cfffd38b9 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -4197,6 +4197,8 @@ void amdgpu_dm_update_connector_after_detect(
 	struct drm_connector *connector = &aconnector->base;
 	struct dc_sink *sink __free(sink_release) = NULL;
 	struct drm_device *dev = connector->dev;
+	struct amdgpu_device *adev = drm_to_adev(dev);
+	int inst;
 
 	/* MST handled by drm_mst framework */
 	if (aconnector->mst_mgr.mst_state == true)
@@ -4330,6 +4332,13 @@ void amdgpu_dm_update_connector_after_detect(
 		/* Set CP to DESIRED if it was ENABLED, so we can re-enable it again on hotplug */
 		if (connector->state->content_protection == DRM_MODE_CONTENT_PROTECTION_ENABLED)
 			connector->state->content_protection = DRM_MODE_CONTENT_PROTECTION_DESIRED;
+
+		mutex_lock(&adev->dm.audio_lock);
+		inst = aconnector->audio_inst;
+		aconnector->audio_inst = -1;
+		mutex_unlock(&adev->dm.audio_lock);
+		if (inst != -1)
+			amdgpu_dm_audio_eld_notify(adev, inst);
 	}
 
 	update_subconnector_property(aconnector);
